  "note": "WEB-HERO-001D reproducibility check for the accepted WEB-HERO-001A/B/C render paths. Phase D extended build_scene.py with a limb_airmass atmosphere profile, an optional day-texture interpolation override, an optional per-object cast_shadow switch and a camera AOI track lock. Each is entered only when a scene spec asks for it, and only hero_predata_animatic does. This record measures that claim rather than asserting it.\n\nMethod. The Cycles plus OptiX GPU path is not bit-reproducible on this machine, so a checksum cannot answer the question, and a difference against a PNG committed in an earlier session confounds a code change with the renderer own session-to-session variation. The accepted Phase-C tree was therefore extracted whole from 6593a80899720f8c7461aaa99ade0e5e63a3ea42 into a scratch workspace, given the same source textures, and rendered in the same session as the current tree. An accepted_vs_current pair then differs in exactly one thing: the Phase-D builder changes.\n\nNoise floor. A single repeat render underestimates the floor. hero_earth_orbit frame 120 first measured 3.0 / 0.012 percent from one repeat pair, which made the accepted_vs_current result look like a regression at 9.0 / 0.087 percent. Rendering that frame three times per tree and cross-comparing every pairing showed the real floor is 9.0 / 0.086 percent, including accepted_vs_accepted at 9.0 / 0.086 percent -- the accepted tree disagreeing with itself by exactly the amount it disagrees with the current tree. The low reading was the outlier, not the high one. The accepted_vs_accepted control is retained below because it is what makes the result conclusive: no comparison involving the Phase-D tree differs from the accepted tree by more than the accepted tree differs from itself.\n\nResult. Every accepted phase rebuilds unchanged. The three accepted scene definitions are also byte-identical in scene.json between that commit and this one; the only scene.json changes are the added hero_predata_animatic entry and the phase field. The committed_evidence_vs_current pairs are retained for continuity with the WEB-HERO-001C record."
